      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t we have to guard this against the lock ? this is what AI suggests me. Just sharing the same here.\n\n\ngunyah_share_range_as_parcels() called gunyah_count_bindings() which\nheld bindings_lock only for the count, then dropped it.  After the\nlock was released, kzalloc() allocated an N-entry parcel array based\non that stale count.  A racing GH_VM_SET_USER_MEM_REGION from another\nthread of the same process could insert K additional bindings before\nthe unlocked mt_for_each() loop ran, causing it to iterate N+K entries\nand write K × ~64 bytes past the end of the N-entry kmalloc\u0027d array.",
      "revId": "93350e5a4e15c802ff1e91151dc7cccd470364f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
